Based on the provided scene images and the ontology vocabulary, here is the semantic interpretation grounded in RDF triples.

### Scene Description in RDF Triples (Turtle Format)

```turtle
@prefix : <http://cecs571.csulb.edu/ontology/cornercase#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

:scene1 a :Scene ;
    :scenarioName "Vehicle view towards intersection with signs and billboards" ;
    :hasCornerCaseType :cc1 .

:cc1 a :StateAnomaly ;
    :hasEvidence :evidence1 ;
    :hasRisk :risk1 ;
    :hasObstacle :roadObstacle1 ;
    :hasWeatherCondition :weather1 .

:evidence1 a :Billboard ;
    :description "Billboards present on the roadside" .

:roadObstacle1 a :RoadObject ;
    :description "Open space with no immediate obstructions" .

:weather1 a :ClearCondition .

:risk1 a :LaneIntrusionRisk ;
    :description "Potential lane intrusion risk due to nearby road users" ;
    :hasSeverityScore :sev1 .

:sev1 a :SeverityScore ;
    :severityValue "0.4"^^xsd:float .
```

